# The snapshot loop itself needs NO secrets: the Wyze tokens are read at runtime
# from the mounted /config/.storage/core.config_entries (the ha-wyzeapi config
# entry), so there is no Wyze password / HA token to configure.
#
# Two OPTIONAL secrets, each gating an opt-in feature; unset either and that
# feature disables itself (the sidecar stays secretless by default). Copy this
# file to .env (gitignored) and fill in only the features you want.
#
# 1. MQTT_PASS -- your broker user's password, enabling the Wyze cloud conn-state
#    bridge: retained wyze/<mac>/status publishing. Host/user/port are non-secret
#    and live in docker-compose.yml.
#
# MQTT_PASS=<broker password>
#
# 2. HA_TOKEN -- a Home Assistant long-lived access token, enabling the
#    event-driven fast path: on a wyze_camera_event the sidecar grabs a fresh
#    still for that one camera immediately instead of waiting up to
#    REFRESH_SECONDS. HA_URL is non-secret (docker-compose.yml).
#
# HA_TOKEN=<HA long-lived access token>  # HA profile -> Long-Lived Access Tokens
#
#    If this token is an ADMIN token you can also set DASH_SYNC=1 in
#    docker-compose.yml to keep the "Cameras" dashboard auto-updated as cameras
#    come and go (creating/saving a Lovelace dashboard is admin-only).
#
# 3. GEMINI_API_KEY -- a Google AI Studio API key, enabling Gemini vision analysis:
#    on a matching event the sidecar pulls a multi-frame burst and sends it to
#    Gemini for a structured description (what's there + what CHANGES across the
#    frames), published to an MQTT-discovery HA sensor. Also needs the MQTT_*
#    publisher (the sensor rides the same broker). Use a PAID-tier key (the free
#    tier trains on your data). NEVER commit the key; it rides in the request
#    query string so the code never logs the request URL.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=<AI Studio API key>
#
# Tunables (otherwise set in docker-compose.yml):
# REFRESH_SECONDS=600     # snapshot cycle; MUST stay < 1800 (KVS cred lifetime)
# FRAME_TIMEOUT=30        # per-camera frame.jpeg HTTP timeout (s)
# FRAME_ATTEMPTS=3        # retries while go2rtc establishes the KVS connection
# GO2RTC_SETTLE=5         # grace after (re)starting go2rtc before pulling frames
# VISION_FRAMES=4         # frames per Gemini burst
# VISION_FRAME_INTERVAL=1.5  # seconds between burst frames
# VISION_MIN_INTERVAL=30  # min seconds between Gemini analyses for the same cam
